# --- Player_task13.events ---
# Task 13: Footstep sounds by material
#
# Part A: `me is moving`          — true only while a move/goto/face is active
# Part B: `when me touches <mat>` — fires on enter-edge contact with a material
# Part C: `play step sound "<mat>"` — plays the mapped clip, cooldown-gated (0.3s)
#
# Setup (do once):
#  1. Create a Physical Material in Content and set its Tag (e.g. "Grass").
#  2. Assign that material to your floor actor's Collider component.
#  3. Import your step-sound clip (e.g. "footstep.wav").
#  4. Map the material to the clip — add this somewhere once (e.g. in Game.events
#     when game starts, or in your player's setup script):
#        var sheet = Runtime.FindActorSheet("Player");
#        sheet.StepSoundMap["Grass"] = "footstep";
#
#    Without StepSoundMap, `play step sound` warns once and skips.

# Walk on Grass → play the grass step sound (only while moving).
when me touches Grass and me is moving
  play step sound "Grass"

# Stand still on Grass → silence (`me is moving` is false).
# Walk from Grass onto Stone → sound switches to Stone on re-entry.
#   when me touches Stone and me is moving
#     play step sound "Stone"
